    <changeSet id="openworkflow-280-draft-definitions-need-not-compile" author="forwardmeasure">
        <comment>A DRAFT revision's source no longer has to compile to be saved - only source_document/
            source_digest (a plain hash of the raw text, computable without compiling) stay mandatory.
            The other eight columns are every field OpenWorkflowCompiler.compile() produces; NULL now
            means "not compiled yet," populated for the first time when the revision is submitted for
            review (compile() failure there still blocks the DRAFT -> IN_REVIEW transition, so nothing
            leaves DRAFT without a clean compile - see the workflow_definition_content_immutable trigger
            above, unaffected: it already only locks these columns once lifecycle_state is no longer
            DRAFT, and IS DISTINCT FROM already treats NULL correctly on both sides.</comment>
        <dropNotNullConstraint tableName="workflow_definition" columnName="resolved_document" columnDataType="TEXT"/>
        <dropNotNullConstraint tableName="workflow_definition" columnName="resolved_resources" columnDataType="TEXT"/>
        <dropNotNullConstraint tableName="workflow_definition" columnName="namespace" columnDataType="VARCHAR(255)"/>
        <dropNotNullConstraint tableName="workflow_definition" columnName="document_version" columnDataType="VARCHAR(128)"/>
